> Key questions (I know there are spoilers on these but I'm interested
> in you all's opinion):
>
> Should I use my (probable) wish from the blessed magic lamp or wait
> longer to see if I will need it?  If so, on what?

I saw that you have no reflection. Personally, I'd wish for silver
dragon scale mail and ditch the blue dragon armor. I generally put
reflection as a top priority as not having it can ruin your day. What
if you run into a black dragon? It's disintegration ray will turn your
samurai into a pile of dust in one turn.

> Should I use excalibur or grayswandir?

Where you are now, Excalibur is all right, but once you get into
Gehennom, Grayswandir might be a consideration because it will do
double damage (silver weapon) against undead, demons, etc., who are
quite large in number down there. As we're talking about weapons here,
seeing how you also use a +2 katana, I'd be on the lookout for a
silver saber. I have a Knight character in progress. He dual-wields
Excalibur and a silver saber and he is knee deep into Gehennom (DL
41). Even though he does not have Grayswandir, I've been able to kill
monsters in a short number of turns. I think my silver saber
compensates for a lack of Grayswandir well, though. And it's nice to
use Excalibur against the vampires to prevent them from taking away my
levels.

> Should I spend my scrolls of enchant weapon/armor, magic marker etc.
> or wait until I get better stuff?

You'll want to wait until you acquire better equipment. The only piece
of armor I see that you use that I may use until ascension is the robe
in case I want to have some good spellcasting capability. If you want
to make use of all those spellbooks you acquired, then enchanting that
robe to +5 to wear that thing all the way to the end is possible.
Otherwise, wait with those enchant armor scrolls. And if you do use
that wish for silver scale, then you can burn those scrolls for it
too. Have to ensure you make those enchant armor scrolls blessed for
maximum benefit. I see you have one potion of holy water (the blessed
potion of water). What you need to do is take those useless potions,
like the paralysis potions, and turn them into potions of water.
Combine all the water potions into a single stack and dip them into
your single holy water to get more. Then you can ensure you have
blessed enchant armor/weapon scrolls. You especially want to bless
that magic marker because blessed magic markers make blessed scrolls.

> What should I genocide?
I prefer liches, vampires, mind flayers and disenchanters. If I am
using a weapon like excalibur, though, then vampires aren't really
high on my priority list. Mind flayers are high, but you may consider
what you lose with that. Their corpses grant permanent increases to
intelligence. Only other way to do that besides potions of gain
ability.

> Since I have polycontrol and polymorph should I try to eat rings or
> something crazy like that?

If you have rings to benefit from by eating them, sure.

> Magic trap dancing and then succubus wrasslin'?

Just ensure you don't have anything out that can be burnt (armor,
scrolls, potions), no gold on hand, and readily prepared to deal with
a horde of monsters spawning around you. If you can do all that, then
dance all you want.
